    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔄 Services Keep-alive\n\nDaily at 03:00 Europe/Rome: `POST /v1/services/keep-alive` on the API.\nEach MAIL provider idle for 30 days sends the owner one check email, through\nitself only, so no provider deactivates an idle key (90 idle days).\n\n**Auth**: header `Authorization: Bearer <API_KEEP_ALIVE_TOKEN>`, the\ncredential *Keep-alive Token* (Header Auth). Wrong or missing → 401.\n\n**Alerts**: Telegram when any provider answers `rejected` or `uncertain`\n(a dead key, a refused send). A failed call (401, 5xx, timeout) fails the\nHTTP node, and Settings → Error Workflow → *Error Handler (global)* reports it.\n\n**URL**: `<keep-alive-url>` is filled on import from `BACKUP_KEEP_ALIVE_URL`\nin /opt/backups/.env.\n\nRunbook: `docs/guides/vps-workflow.md`",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-96, -640],
      "id": "5786bf35-30d6-408a-9d0e-f19d815f6d74",
      "name": "Flow Documentation"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 3 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [-96, -32],
      "id": "a184e831-d804-4ec5-b0e6-c10da492d21b",
      "name": "Daily 03:00"
    },
    {
